{"findings": [{"file": "packages/features/apps/components/CredentialActionsDropdown.tsx", "line": 42, "severity": "medium", "category": "bug", "title": "Cache status not refreshed after deleting cache", "body": "The deleteCache mutation's onSuccess only shows a toast and calls the optional `onSuccess` prop. It never invalidates `utils.viewer.calendars.connectedCalendars`. The disconnect mutation does invalidate it, and that query is configured with `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`. So after a successful delete, the dropdown keeps showing "Cache Status / Last updated" and the delete action for data that no longer exists, until a manual reload."}, {"file": "packages/features/apps/components/CredentialActionsDropdown.tsx", "line": 89, "severity": "low", "category": "bug", "title": "Timestamp formatted with hardcoded en-US locale", "body": "The date is formatted with `new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", ...)`. The surrounding string is localized through `t()`, but the timestamp ignores the user's locale and time-format preference. Non-US users see month/day ordering and a 12h clock regardless of their settings. Use the user's locale (e.g. `i18n.language`) or the existing dayjs/time-format helpers."}, {"file": "packages/app-store/googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts", "line": 1024, "severity": "medium", "category": "perf", "title": "Empty-data updateMany adds a write per cache refresh and may be a no-op", "body": "`SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId(this.credential.id, {})` is called after every cache refresh, which includes every Google webhook notification. That adds an UPDATE across all SelectedCalendar rows of the credential each time.

With empty `data`, Prisma may skip the query entirely or not bump `@updatedAt`, so the stated goal may not even be achieved. The PR notes also say this value isn't displayed anywhere. Remove the call, or set an explicit field if a timestamp is actually needed."}, {"file": "packages/lib/getConnectedDestinationCalendars.ts", "line": 21, "severity": "medium", "category": "api", "title": "UserWithCalendars now requires updatedAt/googleChannelId from all callers", "body": "`allSelectedCalendars` and `userLevelSelectedCalendars` now require `updatedAt` and `googleChannelId`. The function is also re-exported for `@calcom/platform-libraries` as `getConnectedDestinationCalendars`. Any caller that selects only externalId/integration/eventTypeId will now fail type-checking, which includes platform API v2 and other repositories that build this user shape. Only `findUnlockedUserForSession` was updated.

These fields aren't used inside this function, so the type widening looks unnecessary."}, {"file": "packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/calendars/deleteCache.handler.ts", "line": 25, "severity": "low", "category": "bug", "title": "Plain Error thrown instead of TRPCError", "body": "A plain `Error` is thrown when the credential is not found or not owned by the user. tRPC maps it to INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR (500), and the failure is logged as a server error instead of a client authorization/not-found condition. Throw `new TRPCError({ code: "NOT_FOUND" })` (or FORBIDDEN) instead."}, {"file": "packages/prisma/migrations/20250715160635_add_calendar_cache_updated_at/migration.sql", "line": 4, "severity": "low", "category": "doc_defect", "title": "Migration warning comment contradicts the SQL", "body": "The header warns that the required `updatedAt` column was added "without a default value" and that this is "not possible if the table is not empty". The statement actually adds the column with `DEFAULT NOW()`, so it is safe on populated tables. The stale auto-generated warning will mislead anyone reviewing migrations and should be removed."}, {"file": "scripts/test-gcal-webhooks.sh", "line": 68, "severity": "low", "category": "bug", "title": "BSD-only `sed -i ''` breaks on Linux", "body": "`sed -i '' -E ...` is macOS/BSD syntax. On GNU sed (Linux, most CI and dev containers), the `''` is parsed as the sed script and the real expression as a filename, so the env file update fails. `ENV_FILE="../.env"` is also resolved relative to the caller's cwd rather than the script location, so running the script from the repo root writes outside the repo."}, {"file": "apps/web/package.json", "line": 11, "severity": "low", "category": "bug", "title": "dev:cron depends on tsx which is not a declared dependency", "body": "The script now runs `npx tsx`, but `tsx` isn't listed in devDependencies (`ts-node` still is). npx will download tsx at run time, which needs network access and uses an unpinned version, so the command is non-reproducible and fails offline. Add `tsx` as a devDependency, or keep `ts-node`."}, {"file": "packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/calendars/deleteCache.handler.ts", "line": 13, "severity": "low", "category": "test_gap", "title": "No tests for new deleteCache handler or getCacheStatusByCredentialIds", "body": "The new mutation includes an authorization check: it must only delete cache for credentials owned by the caller. The new repository aggregation feeds the UI. Neither has unit tests, so regressions in the ownership check or the credential-to-status mapping would go unnoticed."}]}
